patrone-settings (0.3.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The Theme page has a Font choice: Noto Sans, the font Patrone has used
    until now, or Patrone Sans (the fonts-patrone-sans package), Noto Sans
    with a tailed l and a slashed zero. Each card shows text in its font.
    Picking one changes the family of the interface, document and title
    bar fonts and keeps their sizes; the monospace font stays. A font that
    isn't installed can't be picked, and its card names its package.
  * Royal's picture shows its Start button's P in white, as the taskbar
    now draws it.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.3.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Every theme has title bars of its own in GTK 4 apps: Patrone's pale
    blue-grey, or deep navy with a line of Patrone Blue in the dark style;
    Modern's flat, the window's own color; Studio's soft brushed grey with
    bold titles; Classic's slate and Royal's blue as before. Before, only
    Classic and Royal changed title bars, so picking among the others
    seemed to do nothing to windows.
  * Round, Dots and Glossy title bar buttons keep a gap from the window's
    edge, where File Manager's title bar has no padding of its own.
  * The sign-in entry that writes the account's style sheets runs again:
    GNOME 50's session skips autostart entries with
    X-GNOME-Autostart-Phase, which it had.
  * A clearer icon: a white gear on a Patrone Blue tile, bold enough to
    read at 16 pixels in the Start menu and on the taskbar.
  * The Taskbar page has the taskbar's two new choices, Color (from the
    wallpaper, or the theme's own) and Pin icons (Patrone's, or each
    app's own), where the installed taskbar has them.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:20:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The title bar buttons' style is a setting of its own (title-buttons):
    Wide, Round, Dots, Glossy, or the theme's own. Each style sets every
    part of the buttons in every state, so libadwaita apps, other GTK 4
    apps and GTK 3 apps look the same; before, the buttons looked
    different from one app to the next, and some vanished. Themes keep only
    their title bars (Classic's and Royal's).
  * --set-title-buttons STYLE, and --apply, which an autostart entry runs at
    every sign-in so every account has the styles, and gets new versions
    of them.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The Taskbar page also sets the layout (Left, Centered, Split with Start
    on the left and the apps in the middle, or Top) and the Start button's
    icon (eight to pick from). Themes no longer move the taskbar's buttons.
  * Royal: the old Classic, glossy royal blue with a green Start button, no
    longer saying "start". Classic is now plain and square, with solid
    title bars.
  * --set-theme THEME applies a theme without a window, and
    --export-previews DIR saves the choices' pictures; the package installs
    them in /usr/share/patrone/settings/previews. GNOME Settings' Patrone
    page uses both.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0500

patrone-settings (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First package: Patrone Settings, with a Taskbar page (small, medium or
    large), a Title bar buttons page (top right or top left) and a Theme
    page (Patrone, Modern, Classic, Studio), each choice with a picture.
    Themes restyle the taskbar, and title bars and window buttons in GTK 3
    and GTK 4 apps, through the account's gtk.css.

